'''Lockwax''' is a [[Spells|spell]] that is used to bind scrolls.

== Description ==
Contains an unknown sigil in an inner circle with three lines dividing the outer circle into equal sections. Each section is identical with an arrow like sign with a triangle on the end pointing towards the center of each section. To the right of each arrow are two short lines with one bending at a right angle over the other.

From [[Qifrey|Qifrey's]] reaction, it can be assumed that lockwax is not commonly used, or is only used for protecting powerful or important scrolls.{{Ref|m|50|2}} However, it's not clear on how lockwax works and what level of protection it offers or how to open a scroll bound with it.

== Usage ==
In [[Chapter 50]], [[Easthies]] gives Qifrey a scroll bound with Lockwax with no further explanation.{{Ref|m|50|2}}

In [[Chapter 69]], it is revealed that Qifrey broke the seal and used the [[Amplification Scroll|contents inside]] to aid him in his battle against [[Engendale]].{{Ref|m|69|4}}

